11. The Terms-of-Service Comedy

The clearest satire is supplied by the contracts themselves.

OpenAI tells its users:

* do not infringe other people’s rights;
* do not copy or distribute our service;
* do not reverse engineer our system;
* do not automatically extract our output;
* do not use our output to train a competing model. 

This is a perfectly intelligible commercial position.

It is also astonishingly close to the position creators have spent years asking AI developers to respect:

Do not copy my work without permission.
Do not use it to build a competing commercial product.
Do not extract its economic value at industrial scale.

One cannot help admiring the speed with which Silicon Valley rediscovered intellectual-property theory immediately after acquiring intellectual property worth protecting.

